    description:
      "Product Engineer - AI Platform for Investment Firms\n\nSan Francisco, CA / New York, NY\n\n\n\n\nThe Company:\n\nWe are partnering with an AI platform built specifically for investment firms.\n\nThe platform helps investors turn fragmented proprietary data - including investment memos, models, emails, spreadsheets, deal history and trading data - into searchable, usable intelligence, helping teams surface relevant information faster and make better-informed investment decisions.\n\n\n\n\nThe company has raised a $50M Series A led by Sequoia Capital and is seeing significant inbound demand from leading investment firms.\n\n\n\n\nThe founding team brings experience from two of the most successful technology companies of the last decade. The company’s CEO previously joined Stripe when it had around 40 employees and helped scale its AI/ML function, while the company’s CTO previously joined Notion when it had around 30 employees and contributed through a major period of growth.\n\n\n\n\nStrong customer traction is creating a clear need to expand the engineering team, making this a genuine ground-floor opportunity to join as one of the first 20 engineers.\n\n\n\n\nThe Role:\n\nWe are looking for a strong Product Engineer with full-stack capability.\n\nYou will work across frontend applications, backend systems, data infrastructure and production AI, building products used directly by investment teams.\n\n\n\n\nThere is a significant amount of 0→1 engineering. In a typical week, you might turn a 50-page investment memo into searchable knowledge, design an interface that lets analysts trace AI answers back to source documents, or ship a custom agent workflow based on feedback from a customer that morning.\n\n\n\n\nYou will work directly with customers, understand their workflows firsthand and turn those problems into production software quickly.\n\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Be Building:\n\n * Intuitive user interfaces embedded into investors' daily workflows\n * APIs connecting the platform with ChatGPT, Claude, Excel and custom applications\n * Data ingestion pipelines across PDFs, emails, spreadsheets and structured datasets\n * A unified knowledge engine for fragmented investment data\n * Production-grade LLM products and custom agent workflows\n * Evaluation frameworks for measuring and improving AI reliability\n * Secure and reliable systems for handling sensitive investment data\n * Full-stack applications across React, TypeScript, Python and Node.js\n\n\n\n\nWhat We’re Looking For:\n\n * Experience shipping full-stack products end-to-end\n * Strong React / TypeScript experience\n * Strong Python / Node.js or similar backend experience\n * Experience designing scalable APIs and data models\n * Strong engineering fundamentals and product judgment\n * Interest in productionising AI and building reliable LLM-powered products\n * Ability to work directly with customers and translate problems into software\n * Curiosity about finance and how investors work\n\n\n\n\nWhy Join:\n\nThis is an opportunity to join a $50M Series A AI company at the ground floor, working alongside founders who have already experienced hypergrowth firsthand at Stripe and Notion.\n\nYou will have the opportunity to:\n\n * Join as one of the first 20 engineers\n * Work alongside a founding team with early Stripe and Notion experience\n * Build products for leading investment firms\n * Work across frontend, backend, data and production AI\n * Own major product areas from first principles\n * Collaborate directly with customers to shape what you build\n * Join at a point of strong customer traction and rapid team growth\n * Work in a high-ownership environment with flexibility around office hours\n\n\n\n\nLocation: San Francisco, CA or New York, NY\n\nCompensation: $150K - $300K base",
