      "This is a Fully Remote Job\n\n\n\n\n1. About Our Client:\n\nThis organization operates a platform designed to streamline the onboarding process for financial institutions, addressing the complexity and friction involved in opening accounts and accessing various banking services. By integrating with legacy bank infrastructure, core banking systems, and third-party compliance providers, the platform supports onboarding for a wide range of financial products and services, serving millions of users. The company maintains a fully remote US-based team and seeks to innovate in a traditional industry through technology.\n\n\n\n\n2. About the Opportunity:\n\nThe Software Engineer, Product will play a key role in architecting and developing the platform that powers digital onboarding for financial institutions globally. This position is responsible for building scalable, reliable systems that handle diverse onboarding scenarios, directly impacting millions of users. The role involves close collaboration with customers, product teams, and engineering leadership to translate complex banking requirements into effective technical solutions.\n\n\n\n\n3. Responsibilities:\n\n * Architect and develop features across the full technology stack to manage high scale and complexity\n * Enhance and maintain integrations with legacy banking systems and third-party compliance providers\n * Address technical challenges including multi-tenant architecture, real-time data processing, and ensuring bank-grade reliability\n * Collaborate with major banks to understand and implement unique onboarding requirements\n * Ensure system performance, scalability, and reliability for processing millions of applications across various banking products\n\n\n\n\n4. Requirements:\n\n * Experience with modern web technologies such as React, Node.js, and PostgreSQL\n * Strong system design skills and experience building scalable architectures\n * Ability to translate complex business requirements into elegant technical solutions\n * Focus on balancing technical quality with delivering impactful features\n * Consideration for user experience for both consumers and bank employees\n * Proactive in working directly with customers and iterating based on feedback\n * Desire to own significant product components and influence technical decisions\n * Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or Software Engineering\n * Legal authorization to work in the United States and residence within the continental United States\n\n\n\n\n5. Pay Range and Compensation Package:\n\n * The pay range and compensation package for this role will be determined based on the candidate’s experience, skills, and other relevant factors.\n\n\n\n\n6. Benefits & Perks:\n\n * Equity\n * Sponsored 401(k)\n * Parental leave\n * Fully paid health, vision, and dental insurance\n * Unlimited paid time off\n * Remote work stipend\n * Lifestyle stipend\n * Twice-yearly company retreats\n\n\n\n\nEqual Opportunity Statement:\n\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\n\n\n\n\nNote:\n\nTalentHop is not the Employer of Record (EOR) for this role. Our purpose in this opportunity is to connect exceptional candidates with leading employers. We help job seekers worldwide discover roles that match their goals and guide them to complete their full application directly through the hiring company’s career page or ATS.",
